PROJECT OVERVIEW

Finding relevant remote opportunities can be challenging when listings are spread across different platforms. Findora.dev provides a simple interface for exploring remote jobs, viewing job details, and bookmarking opportunities that users want to revisit.

The project demonstrates frontend development, REST API integration, JavaScript modularization, data persistence, automated testing, and version control.


OBJECTIVES

1.Integrate an external API to retrieve remote job listings.
2.Build a user-friendly interface for browsing opportunities.
3.Allow users to save and remove bookmarked opportunities.
4.Use JSON Server as a mock REST API backend.
5.Demonstrate CRUD operations using HTTP methods.
6.Apply modular JavaScript and automated testing.
7.Practice GitHub project management and deployment workflows.

FEATURES 

1.Explore opportunities: Browse remote job listings retrieved from Remote OK.
2.Search opportunities: Filter listings using available search fields.
3.Bookmark opportunities: Save interesting jobs for later.
4.Saved opportunities: View and remove bookmarked listings.
5.Job details: Follow the provided link to view the original job listing.
6.API communication: Retrieve and manage application data using HTTP requests.
7.Error handling: Display feedback when API operations fail.
8.Responsive interface: Adapt the layout for different screen sizes.

