        Getting Started

Prerequisites

Make sure you have installed:

Node.js

npm

Git

Visual Studio Code or another code editor

1. Clone the repository

git clone YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
cd findora.dev

Replace YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL with your GitHub repository URL.

2. Install dependencies

npm install

3. Start JSON Server

npm run start:api

The local API should be available at:

http://localhost:3000

The saved opportunities endpoint is:

http://localhost:3000/savedJobs

The managed opportunities endpoint is:

http://localhost:3000/managedJobs

Keep the terminal running while using the local API.

4. Run the frontend

Open index.html using VS Code Live Server or another local static web server.

The frontend must be able to reach JSON Server at http://localhost:3000 for local data operations.

API Integration

External API

Findora.dev retrieves remote job listings from:

https://remoteok.com/api

The API integration is implemented in api.js.

Local REST API

JSON Server provides the backend endpoints used to manage application data.

HTTP method

Purpose

GET

Retrieve saved or managed opportunities

POST

Create a new saved or managed opportunity

PUT

Replace an existing managed opportunity

PATCH

Update selected fields, such as application status

DELETE

Remove a saved or managed opportunity

The project uses db.json as its local data store.

Note: JSON Server is used as a mock backend for this project. A deployed version requires a publicly accessible backend URL and persistent storage configured for the hosting platform.

Testing

Jest is used for automated testing.

Run the tests with:

npm test

Generate a coverage report with:

npm run test:coverage

Design

The user interface was designed using Figma before implementation.

The design focuses on:

Clear navigation between Explore, Saved, and About.

Consistent opportunity cards.

Readable typography and spacing.

A cohesive blue-and-neutral color scheme.

Responsive layouts for different screen sizes.

